---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../consts';
---
<Base title="Cookie Policy"
      description="What cookies and similar technologies App-Tipps.com may use, what each category does, and how consent will be handled when optional services are enabled.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 24 August 2026.</p>

      <p>
        Cookies and similar technologies can store or read information on a device. This page explains
        the categories App-Tipps may use. For how we handle personal data generally, see our
        {' '}<a href="/cookies-privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Current site state</h2>
      <p>
        App-Tipps currently uses Google Analytics 4 for audience measurement and may serve advertising
        through Google Ad Manager or Google AdSense. A Google-certified consent platform is enabled for
        visitors in regions where Google requires it, and optional storage remains disabled until the
        required choice has been collected.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookie categories</h2>
      <h3>Strictly necessary</h3>
      <p>
        Technologies that are required to deliver, secure or operate the website. These do not depend on
        advertising or analytics preferences and may be used where they are necessary for the service.
      </p>
      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        Audience measurement can tell us which pages are read and how visitors reach the site. If we
        enable analytics that requires consent, it will remain off until the required choice has been
        collected.
      </p>
      <h3>Advertising</h3>
      <p>
        Advertising providers may use cookies or similar identifiers to deliver ads, limit repetition and
        measure performance. Personalised advertising may involve additional processing to infer interests.
        Where consent is required, these technologies will not be enabled before that consent is obtained.
      </p>
      <h3>Affiliate tracking</h3>
      <p>
        Some articles may link to merchants or services through affiliate programmes. When you follow an
        affiliate link, the destination provider may use its own tracking technology so a purchase or
        signup can be attributed to App-Tipps. That technology is controlled by the destination provider
        and is subject to its own policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Google advertising consent</h2>
      <p>
        If Google AdSense or Google Ad Manager is enabled for visitors in the European Economic Area, the
        United Kingdom or Switzerland, App-Tipps will use a Google-certified consent management platform
        integrated with the IAB Europe Transparency and Consent Framework where Google requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changing your choices</h2>
      <p>
        When optional services that require consent are enabled, the site will provide a way to review or
        change those choices. You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
